  "content": "ARTICLE\\_START\\_SENTINEL Reliable extraction begins with preserved evidence. This article contains enough ordinary prose to distinguish useful material from a navigation list. We compare source documents with their cleaned text rather than trusting a successful process exit.\n\n## Methods and observations\n\nMIDDLE\\_SENTINEL Unicode should survive intact: café, naïve, 日本語, and an em dash — without invented translation. The [reference guide](https://example.com/reference) is a relative link whose destination must stay attached to its label. A parser should retain actual observations and keep their wording unchanged.\n\n```python\nprint(\"hello, extraction\")\nprint(7)\n```\n\n| Sample | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| granite | stable |\n| clay | flexible |\n\nARTICLE\\_END\\_SENTINEL These findings conclude the document. Keeping the final paragraph matters because extraction can appear successful while silently dropping later sections. The fixture is not a live article and makes no factual claim about a particular website.",
